# Campaigns: results, schedules, open/click tracking, mailbox health and the audit log.

@token = PASTE-AN-ADMIN-DEV-TOKEN
@workflowId = PASTE-A-WORKFLOW-ID

### Campaign results: funnel, per-step counts with branches, top links
GET {{baseUrl}}/automation/workflows/{{workflowId}}/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Schedule: only from 1 Oct, Monday to Thursday (recipient local days), until 30 Nov
PUT {{baseUrl}}/automation/workflows/{{workflowId}}/schedule
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "start_date": "2026-10-01",
  "end_date": "2026-11-30",
  "weekdays": [1, 2, 3, 4]
}

### Clear the schedule (send whenever the guardrails allow)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/automation/workflows/{{workflowId}}/schedule
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

null

### Open and click tracking (HTML emails only)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/settings/sending
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "track_opens": true,
  "track_clicks": true
}

### Mailbox health of every agent (worst first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/senders/health
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Audit log (admins): everything, or one area by action prefix
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-events?limit=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Only schedule changes
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-events?action=set_workflow_schedule
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# The pixel (/t/o/{token}) and tracked links (/t/c/{token}) are public: they are put into
# emails at send time and carry a signed token. Try one from an outbox email's HTML.
